{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification automata encode the safe, efficient exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, directed recovery (short turns). Full scans are reserved for repeated or persistent blockages. All transitions are deterministic, and every state is total on uncontrollables. No state reached by obstacle events enables forward or random_walk. Recovery states are one-shot and return to exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to allow modular specification.",
    "Specification automata bind perception outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
